{"id":"chatcmpl-bb58d6d2-2766-4b58-b488-3efb67556102","object":"chat.completion","created":1795229712,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"When automated expert models return negative or ambiguous results on a forced-choice medical imaging question, the correct strategy is to escalate to independent verification tools (grounded reports, phrase grounding) rather than trusting the first negative. Localization/grounding tools can resolve subtle findings that classification-style experts miss, and the final answer should be anchored to the tool that provides spatial evidence consistent with one of the offered options.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a specialized expert model returns a negative/uncertain result on a forced-choice question, treat it as a potential false negative and cross-check with an independent verification tool before concluding.\",\n    \"Use spatial grounding/localization tools to confirm subtle findings that classification or report tools may under-report, since coordinates provide positive evidence for one option over another.\",\n    \"When the question format guarantees one option is correct, a 'no finding' response from any single model should trigger escalation to alternate evidence sources rather than acceptance.\",\n    \"Anchor the final answer to the tool whose output (e.g., localized region) is consistent with exactly one of the provided options, using that consistency as the deciding signal.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging forced-choice QA\": \"Chain expert classification -> grounded report -> phrase grounding; treat negatives as suspect and let localization break ties.\",\n    \"Ambiguous/negative model outputs\": \"Escalate to a second and third independent tool when the first returns 'no' on a question that presupposes a positive finding.\",\n    \"Evidence-based answer selection\": \"Prefer the option supported by spatially specific evidence (coordinates/regions) over generic yes/no outputs.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm whether any tool returned spatially specific evidence (localization/coordinates) matching exactly one option.\",\n    \"Verify that a negative expert result was cross-checked with at least one independent verification tool before finalizing.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":535,"total_tokens":928,"completion_tokens":393,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":535},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":393}}}